``

So the on-disk slug layout is shared with pi-mono. Changing the encoding scheme would make new session folders use a different scheme than pi's. Hmm. But the bug says it's irreversibly lossy. There's tension:

1. Changing encode to percent-encoding breaks compatibility with pi-mono's on-disk scheme and with existing sessions on disk (they live under old-style slug dirs). New sessions would be created under NEW-style slug dirs — that's actually fine for sessions since each session file's header holds the real cwd, and `list()` reads headers, not slugs. But cross-tool compatibility (pi's own session resume browsing this repo) might matter.

